      "strengths_deep_dive": [
        "OBAT Helpers demonstrates a robust commitment to organizational health and transparency. The charity's <cite id=\"15\">100% independent board of 22 members</cite> ensures strong oversight and governance. Financially, the organization is resilient, maintaining <cite id=\"16\">5.7 months of working capital</cite> to sustain operations during funding fluctuations. Their fundraising efficiency is also notable, spending only <cite id=\"17\">$0.06 to raise every $1</cite> in FY2024, which significantly beats common industry benchmarks. This efficiency allows more resources to be directed toward their <cite id=\"18\">50 educational and training projects</cite> and <cite id=\"19\">3 health clinics</cite> serving displaced populations."
      ],
      "summary": "OBAT Helpers is a dedicated humanitarian organization that has worked since <cite id=\"1\">its founding in 2004</cite> to empower displaced and marginalized communities in Bangladesh. The charity focuses on breaking the cycle of poverty through <cite id=\"2\">education, healthcare, and empowerment initiatives</cite> specifically targeting residents of internally displaced person (IDP) camps and Rohingya refugees. With <cite id=\"3\">$2,184,558 in total revenue in FY2023</cite>, the organization maintains a significant operational footprint, providing <cite id=\"4\">direct services to over 13,703 families</cite>. OBAT Helpers is distinguished by its high level of transparency, holding a <cite id=\"5\">Platinum Seal of Transparency from Candid</cite> and an <cite id=\"6\">overall score of 90.90.33333333333333/100 from Charity Navigator</cite>. While the organization faced a <cite id=\"7\">revenue decline of 27% in FY2024</cite>, it continues to deliver high-impact services with a <cite id=\"8\">program expense ratio of 82.1%</cite>. The charity is <cite id=\"9\">verified as zakat-eligible</cite>, making it a reliable choice for Muslim donors seeking to support the <cite id=\"10\">fuqara (poor) and masakin (needy)</cite> through established educational and medical programs.",
